    {
      "id": 228362,
      "name": "bolnerap",
      "username": "bolnerap",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bolnerap/{size}/6056_2.png",
      "created_at": "2019-08-06T21:52:03.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Mint at 10 / 11 / 9. Like eugeneruss, I had Tempest set up with Shackles/Hailstorm... eventually. For several rounds, it was all damage control, as I set up Medico with Universal Donor and Akash was on Ongoing destruction duty. Bottom of the 9th also helped us get some extra card plays out so Ermine didn't get to affect us that much. Once both copies of Bugbear's DR were destroyed, Tempest went nuts and wiped the field.</p>\n<p>Akash also made things easier when a Creeping Mold from the environment deck let her dump her (sizeable thanks to Bottom of the 9th hitting a draw 5) hand and picking up two As The Earth Turns. Only needed one of them to completely neutralize the enemies for one round for Tempest to wail on them. All three of them dropped on the same Tempest turn.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:02:50.106Z",
